      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-549",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{c}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3c}{2} \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
